      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we need to find the volume of the original pyramid and subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid.\n\nWe know that the volume of a pyramid is given by:\n\nV = (1/3)Bh\n\nwhere B is the area of the base, and h is the altitude.\n\nFor the original pyramid with base edge 12 cm and altitude 8 cm:\n\nV_original = (1/3)(base_edge^2) * altitude = (1/3)(12^2) * 8 = 384 cm³\n\nFor the smaller pyramid with base edge 6 cm and altitude 4 cm:\n\nV_smaller = (1/3)(base_edge^2) * altitude = (1/3)(6^2) * 4 = 48 cm³\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the difference between the volume of the original pyramid and the smaller pyramid:\n\nV_frustum = V_original - V_smaller = 384 - 48 = 336 cm³\n\nThus, the volume of the frustum is \\boxed{336} cubic centimeters.",
