      "text": "To determine the volume of the frustum, we need to find the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid (which will be combined with a taller frustum to form the original pyramid). The volume of the frustum can then be calculated by subtracting the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the volume of the original pyramid. The volume \\(V\\) of a pyramid is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height} \\]\nFor the original pyramid:\n- The base edge is 12 cm, so the base area is \\(12^2 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\\).\n- The height is 8 cm.\nSo the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid. We know the base edge is 6 cm and the height is 4 cm. So the volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 6^2 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nThe volume of the frustum is the volume of the original pyramid minus the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculating the volume of the original pyramid\r\nbase_edge_original = 12\r\nheight_original = 8\r\n\r\n# Base area of the original pyramid\r\nbase_area_original = base_edge_original ** 2\r\n\r\n# Volume of the original pyramid\r\nvolume_original = (1/3) * base_area_original * height_original\r\n\r\n# Calculating the volume of the smaller pyramid\r\nbase_edge_small = 6\r\nheight_small = 4\r\n\r\n# Base area of the smaller pyramid\r\nbase_area_small = base_edge_small ** 2\r\n\r\n# Volume of the smaller pyramid\r\nvolume_small = (1/3) * base_area_small * height_small\r\n\r\n# Volume of the frustum\r\nvolume_frustum = volume_original - volume_small\r\nprint(volume_frustum)\n```\n```output\n336.0\n```\nThe volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{336}\\) cubic centimeters.",
